      "writtenOn": "2026-07-06T17:23:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I ended up creating `withPrimitiveColor` as a non-static function since to me if its taking in a PaintParams as the first argument it makes sense to be a member function, just marked it const for clarity that its constructing a new PaintParams. I think this is clearer than adding another constructor variant as well.\n\nThis let me condense down the code for the `primitiveBlender` and `primitiveColorOverride` into a single ternary. IMO the ternary isn\u0027t the clearest to read but other ways I\u0027ve tried formatting it I\u0027ve found I would either evaluate the condition twice, create the blender singleton even if not used, or create a copy of the `baseParams` when it could be taken as a reference.",
